You probably don't.

00:38:29.060 --> 00:38:29.960
[CHIMES]

00:38:29.960 --> 00:38:32.540
So we have a very, very cool
way that you can actually

00:38:32.540 --> 00:38:34.430
take your Cloud
Shell environment

00:38:34.430 --> 00:38:36.740
and spin it up
using a Docker image

00:38:36.740 --> 00:38:38.300
that you can build yourself.

00:38:38.300 --> 00:38:40.200
And it pretty much
involves two steps.

00:38:40.200 --> 00:38:42.597
The first step is to
create the Docker image

00:38:42.597 --> 00:38:43.805
of which you need to include.

00:38:43.805 --> 00:38:45.590
So you want Terraform and Helm.

00:38:45.590 --> 00:38:47.630
You can just create
your Docker file,

00:38:47.630 --> 00:38:50.300
include the steps to
install Terraform and Helm,

00:38:50.300 --> 00:38:52.250
and then go ahead
and build that image.

00:38:52.250 --> 00:38:54.243
Then you push it up to
the Container Registry.

00:38:54.243 --> 00:38:56.660
And in Cloud Shell, you can
go to the environment settings

00:38:56.660 --> 00:38:58.520
and just choose
that container right

00:38:58.520 --> 00:39:00.320
from the Container Registry.

00:39:00.320 --> 00:39:03.630
And then Cloud Shell will boot
into using that container.

00:39:03.630 --> 00:39:05.810
So if you have a long,
complicated setup process,

00:39:05.810 --> 00:39:08.060
or even if you just
want a few extra tools,

00:39:08.060 --> 00:39:11.010
you can quickly, quickly
put that image together

00:39:11.010 --> 00:39:12.200
and then boot from that.

00:39:12.200 --> 00:39:13.850
And you have everything
you need to go.

